## DET.PROSE.LENGTH implemented

Implemented the deterministic prose-length check. Shell commands were unavailable in this session, so **`npm run blend-rules` and `npm test` need to be run locally** to refresh the registry fingerprint and confirm the suite.

### Plan (signals from rule anchor)

From `docs/design/ux-audit/deterministic-design-rules.md#det-prose-length` and `forge-enterprise-ai-website-standard.md`:

| Signal | Threshold | Source |
|--------|-----------|--------|
| Paragraph word count | ≤ **85** words | Legacy `readability-structure` + enterprise “1–2 paragraphs per section” |
| Card list items | ≤ **3** direct `li` | Enterprise “Bullets per card: 3 maximum” |
| Main prose lists | ≤ **12** direct `li` | Scannability cap for non-nav lists |

Platform handbook inner pages are skipped (same as legacy readability checks).

### Do — `det-prose-length.check.js`

- **`longParagraphViolations()`** — uses existing `metrics.paragraphs` from DOM metrics (no extra crawl cost).
- **`collectProseLengthReport()`** — Playwright `page.evaluate` for `ul`/`ol` in `main`, excluding nav/TOC/sidebar; separate card vs prose caps.
- **`findingsFromLongParagraphs()` / `findingsFromListLengthReport()`** — testable pure helpers.
- **`run({ metrics, page, url, ctx })`** — merges metrics + optional live list scan; thresholds overridable via `ctx.maxParagraphWords`, `ctx.maxCardListItems`, `ctx.maxProseListItems`.
- Finding shape preserved: `severity`, `area: 'readability'`, `message`, `evidence`, `remediation`.

### Register — `rule-mappings.js`

`DET.PROSE.LENGTH` is registered under `DETERMINISTIC_IMPLEMENTATIONS` as **implemented**:

- `area`: `readability`
- `scoreDimension`: `depthAndTechnicalDisclosure` (matches legacy `technical-depth` / `readability-structure` adapters)
- `priorityWeight`: `7`
- `defaultSeverity`: `minor`

### Check — tests added

New file: `auditor-tests/det-prose-length.test.js` covering constants, paragraph/list violations, handbook skip, aggregation, and `run()`.

